{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:26:47.273592Z","id":"2449beb4de0fac8b66304aea93dfeb249c13fd7cb9355759ae701a4d6b97968d","body":{"detail":"The classification closure in `share_all` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1395-1403) returns `UploadState::New` for everything under `--force` and otherwise the manifest's verdict; the upload loop (cmd_share.rs:1448-1450) skips anything that is not `New`, so `Changed` sessions are never uploaded by `--all`. The doc comment on `share_all` (cmd_share.rs:1324-1331) and CLAUDE.md:227 leave changed sessions to `path sync`, but no `path sync` remote-update command exists in this tree (`RemoteState`'s own comment at crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:76-78 says sync 'will add its own fields here … as it lands'). Today a user with N uploaded sessions of which M changed has exactly one way to get the M up: `--force`, which also creates N-M duplicate graphs of sessions that were already current — the duplication the skip rule exists to prevent. The hint printed at cmd_share.rs:1421 ('pass --force to upload everything again') points at that. Single `share` on the same session takes the opposite decision: `UploadState::Changed` at cmd_share.rs:904-909 prints 'session changed since, uploading a new graph' and uploads without `--force`. So the same changed session is uploaded by `path share --harness x --session y` and skipped by `path share --all`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1395},"end":{"line":1403},"content_hash":"c887b26e335d87dc4b376cfe16352c96db11e8a19e72c13307867de2e55b4568"},"suggested_fix":"Until a `path sync` remote update exists, make `--all` treat `Changed` like single `share` does (upload a new graph, keep counting it separately in the summary), or add a changed-only override (e.g. `--force` uploads `Changed`, a separate flag or `--force --force`-style option re-uploads `Uploaded`). Whichever is chosen, make the `Nothing to upload` hint name the option that uploads only the changed sessions, and add a mock-server test asserting a changed session's fate under `--all` without `--force`.","summary":"`share --all` never uploads a session classified Changed, and the only override (`--force`) re-uploads every unchanged session too — there is no changed-only path, and single `share` behaves differently","tags":["review","review:pr-355-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:26:47.273718Z","id":"508137bbe0e5f62254854acca972fcd83db0afeed76a7eedd10b6bb23e600803","body":{"detail":"`ProjectScope::admits` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:98-104) routes `Under` through `crate::sync::sources::project_in_scope`, which for claude is `claude_project_in_scope` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/sources.rs:177-188): both sides are slugged with `s.replace(['/', '_', '.'], \"-\")` and matched by `p == parent || p.starts_with(parent + \"-\")`. With `--project-under /w/foo` (slug `-w-foo`) the project `/w/foo_bar` (slug `-w-foo-bar`) starts with `-w-foo-` and is admitted; the same holds for `/w/foo.old`; pi's `pi_project_in_scope` (sources.rs:475-486) replaces only `/`, so under `/w/foo` it admits `/w/foo-bar`. CLAUDE.md:242 documents this as a known property of `p cache sync`, where an over-match costs a local cache derive. In `share --all` the over-match is an upload of someone else's project's sessions to the subtree's destination, which is not reversible from the CLI. This PR gives the claude and pi rows the real recorded directory (`ArtifactRow.cwd`, set at cmd_share.rs:241 and cmd_share.rs:344 from `ConversationMetadata.cwd` / `SessionMeta.cwd`), so an exact check is now possible for every session that recorded a cwd; `collect_claude` still decides admission on the lossy `project` string at cmd_share.rs:223 before reading metadata and never re-checks the row's `cwd`.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":98},"end":{"line":104},"content_hash":"a6f39692a675557fbbbfa9f6fb7801ef90e0f0845b98b227ad0e8bf989158d42"},"suggested_fix":"Keep the slug-space pre-filter on the project directory (it is cheap and a superset), then in `collect_claude`/`collect_pi` drop a row whose `cwd` is `Some` and fails `dir_in_scope(cwd, under)` when the scope is `Under`. `enumerate_stamps` can keep using the slug-space `enumerate(project_under)`: a superset of stamps is harmless. Add a `gather_artifacts` test with slugs `-w-foo` and `-w-foo-bar` whose sessions record cwd `/w/foo` and `/w/foo_bar`, asserting `Under(\"/w/foo\")` yields only the first.","summary":"`ProjectScope::Under` admits claude and pi sessions from sibling directories whose names differ only by `_`/`.` (claude) or `-` (pi) — a slug-space match, so `share --all --project-under ~/w/foo` bulk-uploads `~/w/foo_bar` and `~/w/foo.old` sessions too","tags":["review","review:pr-355-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:26:47.273820Z","id":"9dd5ecad4c7763ce1184fd6bd16581c853837f069fc2dd0bfc907b07bab2eb88","body":{"detail":"`load_session` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1077-1090) takes `fresh_cache_id_in` at its word and `read_to_string`s the cache path, turning a missing file into `Failed to read …`. The sync engine's equivalent gate, `is_unchanged` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:247-257), additionally requires `cache_path(id).exists()` before trusting a record — CLAUDE.md:241 states 'sync verifies doc files actually exist before skipping'. `p cache rm` downgrades records so this does not trigger through the CLI, but a manual removal of the cache directory (or a cache directory moved out from under an unchanged manifest) leaves every record pointing at a missing file. For single `share` that is one clear error; for `share --all` it is one `failed: Failed to read …` line per session and a non-zero exit, with nothing uploaded, although the derive that would fix it is one step away.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1077},"end":{"line":1090},"content_hash":"8d33271a3cba687521115430e7c87d1696a1a632ff2e725f38c817c0979e9d4b"},"suggested_fix":"In `load_session`, treat a missing cache document as a cache miss: if `cache_path(&cache_id)` does not exist (or the read fails with `NotFound`), fall through to the derive branch rather than returning the error. A unit test: record a fresh manifest entry, delete the cache file, call `load_session` and assert `LoadOrigin::Derived`.","summary":"`load_session` errors instead of deriving when the manifest's cache entry is fresh but its document file is gone; under `--all` that fails every session of a wiped cache","tags":["review","review:pr-355-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:26:47.273939Z","id":"c16aeda17071417e7671d71ea5dcd4604a4e80746c5b7b95b402fd80ebd2fd71","body":{"detail":"The closure at crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1373-1393 is where `share --all` decides a configured remote's `BulkTarget`, including `base_url: match (&args.url, found.base_url) { (None, Some(remote_url)) => remote_url, _ => base_url }` at cmd_share.rs:1386-1389 — the value `BulkTarget::remote()` (cmd_share.rs:1135-1137) turns into the manifest key that every later skip decision depends on. The PR's mock-server tests (cmd_share.rs:2638-2821) all run with no `~/.toolpath/config.toml`, so they only ever exercise the `pathstash` default; the `plan_bulk` unit tests (cmd_share.rs:1999-2063) pass `|_| Ok(None)` or a hard-coded closure in place of this one. Untested as a result: that a URL-form `[[project]]` remote records the upload under the remote's own server rather than the login server; that a rerun with the same config skips; that `--url` overrides the embedded server for both the upload and the key; and that `--repo` disables the lookup (cmd_share.rs:1374-1376).","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1373},"end":{"line":1393},"content_hash":"c4ee332e9f21d26ef7495d9f5f394006f434ed87c6ec9bddd6c88c4232d1bc84"},"suggested_fix":"Add one mock-server test in the `with_home` style that writes a `~/.toolpath/config.toml` with a `[[project]] dir = \"/test/project\" remote = \"<mock base>/u/me/proj\"` rule, runs `share_all` twice, and asserts the request path hits `/u/me/repos/proj/graphs`, the manifest key is `remote_key(<mock base>, \"me\", \"proj\")`, and the rerun sends nothing; a variant with `--url` asserts the key follows the flag.","summary":"The real remote-resolution closure in `share_all` — `[[project]]` lookup, embedded-server vs `--url` choice, memoization — has no end-to-end test; every `plan_bulk` test stubs it","tags":["review","review:pr-355-r1","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:32:55.040850Z","id":"d1231f7fe05c7f45811d42d80c0728a003a918b05442653476337040497fe036","body":{"detail":"`ProjectScope::admits` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:98-104) sends `Under` to `crate::sync::sources::project_in_scope`, which dispatches claude to `claude_project_in_scope` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/sources.rs:177-188): `slug(s) = s.replace(['/', '_', '.'], \"-\")`, matched by `p == *parent || p.starts_with(&format!(\"{parent}-\"))`. slug(\"/w/foo\") = \"-w-foo\"; slug(\"/w/foo_bar\") = \"-w-foo-bar\" and slug(\"/w/foo.old\") = \"-w-foo-old\", both of which start with \"-w-foo-\", so both are admitted. `pi_project_in_scope` (sources.rs:475-486) replaces only '/', so under \"/w/foo\" (\"-w-foo\") the project \"/w/foo-bar\" (\"-w-foo-bar\") is admitted. `collect_claude` decides admission on the lossy `project` string at cmd_share.rs:223 (`if !admits(scope, ArtifactType::Claude, Some(&project))`) before `list_conversation_metadata`, and the row's real `cwd` (set at cmd_share.rs:241 from `m.cwd`, and for pi at cmd_share.rs:344) is never re-checked against the scope. The only scope test, `gather_artifacts_project_under_admits_subtree` (cmd_share.rs:1975-1987), uses `-work-foo`, `-work-foo-sub`, `-other` under `/work` and so does not exercise a sibling collision. In `share_all` (cmd_share.rs:1345-1346) this scope selects the rows that are uploaded. Over-match requires specific sibling naming, so `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"508137bbe0e5f62254854acca972fcd83db0afeed76a7eedd10b6bb23e600803","summary":"confirmed: ProjectScope::Under matches claude in slug space and pi in '-'-encoded space, so --project-under /w/foo admits /w/foo_bar, /w/foo.old (claude) and /w/foo-bar (pi) sessions into the bulk upload","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:32:55.040866Z","id":"7db4a2750e5d646c0732da09c2177ad122298d3f49fc5243bd7bdb3e9e603dff","body":{"detail":"`crate::sync::fresh_cache_id_in` (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:481-496) returns the cache id only when `(rec.modified.is_some() || rec.size.is_some()) && rec.modified == modified && rec.size == size && crate::cache::cache_path(&cache_id).is_ok_and(|p| p.exists())` (engine.rs:491-495). With the document file missing that condition is false and the function returns `None`, so the `if let Some(cache_id) = crate::sync::fresh_cache_id_in(...)` branch in `load_session` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1077-1088) is not taken and control falls through to `derive_session` at cmd_share.rs:1090, which rewrites the cache via `write_cached(.., true)` at cmd_share.rs:1096. The `read_to_string` at cmd_share.rs:1081 can therefore only fail on a file that existed at the `exists()` check and disappeared or became unreadable before the read, not on a wiped or moved cache directory. This is the same existence check the sync engine's `is_unchanged` applies (engine.rs:247-257) and that `record_is_current` applies (engine.rs:474).","kind":"comment","references":"9dd5ecad4c7763ce1184fd6bd16581c853837f069fc2dd0bfc907b07bab2eb88","summary":"refuted: fresh_cache_id_in already requires the cache document file to exist, so a wiped cache directory makes load_session derive, not error","tags":["verified:refuted","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:32:55.040876Z","id":"b4d6e35e4843121fd7b0685ea635c34a3f6a6a74848a5aff7df7a78af64ce7ed","body":{"detail":"The resolve closure lives at crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1373-1393 (`if args.repo.is_some() { return Ok(None); }` at 1374-1376; `crate::share_config::resolve_remote(...)` at 1382; `base_url: match (&args.url, found.base_url) { (None, Some(remote_url)) => remote_url, _ => base_url.clone() }` at 1386-1389). `BulkTarget::remote()` (cmd_share.rs:1135-1137) turns that into the manifest key passed to `upload_state` at cmd_share.rs:1398-1402. In the test module, `config.toml` with `[[project]]` rules is written exactly once, at cmd_share.rs:2438-2446, inside `destination_applies_configured_remote`, which calls `resolve_destination` (the single-share path), not `share_all`. The mock-server tests (`with_home`, cmd_share.rs:2560-2582; `run_all`, 2593-2601) pin `$TOOLPATH_CONFIG_DIR` to an empty tempdir and write no config, so every `share_all` run resolves to the `pathstash` default. The two `plan_bulk` unit tests pass `|_| Ok(None)` (cmd_share.rs:2008) and a hard-coded `Ok((dir == \"/w/foo\").then(|| target(\"me\", \"foo\")))` (cmd_share.rs:2031-2034). None of the listed behaviours (URL-form remote keying the record under the remote's server, rerun skip with the same config, `--url` override of the embedded server, `--repo` disabling lookup) is asserted anywhere in `share_all`'s tests. Test gap, not an observed defect; `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"c16aeda17071417e7671d71ea5dcd4604a4e80746c5b7b95b402fd80ebd2fd71","summary":"confirmed: no test runs share_all against a [[project]] config; the mock-server tests use no config.toml and every plan_bulk test substitutes the resolve closure","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:32:55.040887Z","id":"58ed6a410471ef2b1c4ee5d8d3bb319dfe7357910b8a1eab72dbd07aab5028af","body":{"detail":"The classification closure in `share_all` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs:1395-1403) returns `UploadState::New` when `args.force` and otherwise `crate::sync::upload_state(...)`; the upload loop skips with `if !matches!(state, UploadState::New) { continue; }` at cmd_share.rs:1448-1450, so `Changed` rows are never uploaded by `--all`. Under `--force` every row is `New`, so unchanged rows are re-uploaded too; the hint at cmd_share.rs:1421 is 'Nothing to upload; pass --force to upload everything again.' The test `share_all_leaves_a_changed_session_alone_until_forced` (cmd_share.rs:2675-2710) pins this: after the session grows, a second `run_all` leaves the record unchanged and only `force: true` uploads. Single `share` differs: `share_explicit`'s match at cmd_share.rs:893-911 handles `UploadState::Changed(u)` by printing 'session changed since, uploading a new graph' and continuing to the upload without `--force`; only `Uploaded(u) if !args.force` returns early. The deferral to `path sync` in the doc comment (cmd_share.rs:1324-1331) and CLAUDE.md:227 has no implementation in this tree: the only `Sync` subcommand is `p cache sync` (crates/path-cli/src/cmd_cache.rs:33), a local cache fill, and `RemoteState`'s comment (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:76-78) says sync 'will add its own fields here ... as it lands'. Deliberate design gap rather than a defect; `concern` is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"2449beb4de0fac8b66304aea93dfeb249c13fd7cb9355759ae701a4d6b97968d","summary":"confirmed: share --all skips every UploadState::Changed row and --force is the only override, which also re-uploads unchanged rows; single share uploads a Changed session without --force","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/cmd_share.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-07T16:33:49.554853Z","id":"bc937a84ffb0e671353c7da037b91609118009697af8bc134741ca6bdefc63be","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Refuted by verification reply 7db4a2750e5d646c0732da09c2177ad122298d3f49fc5243bd7bdb3e9e603dff: fresh_cache_id_in (crates/path-cli/src/sync/engine.rs:491-495) already requires the cache document to exist, so a missing file falls through to derive_session.","supersedes":"9dd5ecad4c7763ce1184fd6bd16581c853837f069fc2dd0bfc907b07bab2eb88","tags":["reason:invalid","session:claude-code:e7a0e4d4-d193-4368-8056-1808f5a5eacd"]}}
